\heading{2}{References}

As demonstrated by \cite{knuth1984}, the separation of content
and presentation is a foundational concept in document processing.
See \heading{1}{Introduction} \ref{sec:intro} for more details.

\heading{1}{Conclusion}

This example demonstrates the core features of the VernierOffice
document language. The language provides a minimal but complete
set of semantic constructs for document authoring.

